lank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T10:16:13-08:00","id":1041326,"title":"","content":"I'm going to break my earlier &quot;go for strong themes mote than fun settings!&quot; rule from earlier and say that Victorian Hong Kong and 1830s occupied Shanghai would both be incredible kitchen sink crossover settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T10:17:15-08:00","id":1041328,"title":"","content":"Someone will probably point out that a writer has already said otherwise, but I imagine if we're ever going to get a kitchen sink setting, it would be in the Crossover Book, which would show examples of said crossover in said kitchen sink setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T10:41:01-08:00","id":1041337,"title":"","content":"Mayhaps Chicago 2E?<br /> <br /> I also thought of the song (They Might be Giants version thanks to the Tiny Toons <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T10:45:48-08:00","id":1041338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041323#post1041323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vsQrKZcYtqg\" data-code=\"vsQrKZcYtqg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/vsQrKZcYtqg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> (Not sorry, if my Islamic History Professor can get away with showing this in class, its fair game)<br /> <br /> To be fair, Istanbul has such a storied history that it could easily fit another Demon era (or two or three) in after everyone starts calling it Istanbul consistently.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is perfectly within Demon's themes to have multiple instances of the City named Istandul and Constantonpole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T10:45:49-08:00","id":1041339,"title":"","content":"Here's a few pitches, I'll add more later...<br /> <br /> <b>Qin Dynasty Vampire: </b>Covenants that rose of the Hundred Schools of Thought. The Legalist Covenant (which in addition to bureaucratic governance of vampires is also the culture's &quot;we are monsters who are supposed to keep humanity in line through fear&quot; faction) is beginning to enforce 'Shu' (the Masquerade) on the rest of the Kindred. The Confucian Covenant (feudal rule + serving as active &quot;ancestors&quot; with filial relationships with living family and necromantically with the passed) is fighting back HARD. Meanwhile a Taoist Covenant explores the mysteries of Blood Alchemy. If the chapter is expanded, it incorporates &quot;Immortals&quot; updates for 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> <b>Wolves of Bau (2nd Editon)</b>: Updated with the revelation of how (relatively) recent the Sundering was, this setting is represented as being before/during the Oaths of the Moon. The rulership of Bau is a failed attempt for the Uratha to carve out a place for themselves in the world before turning instead to readopting Father Wolf's cause. The Oaths of the Moon are presented as a Rite that exists in the setting, readopting the lost auspices at the cost of losing the special advantages of the Bau setting.<br /> <br /> <b>Underground Railroad Changeling:</b> The thematic link is obvious, and the (dangerous) use of Trods to facilitate the escape of slaves opens tons of plot potential. You also get the veneer of of &quot;Antebellum romance&quot; with appropriate focus on the real darkness of the era. With expansion, I'd incorporate it Brazil, Dahomey &amp; Abeokuta, linked by Trods along lines of the Wyrd to the US's underground as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Haundenosaunee Hunter: </b>Set during the birth of the Haudenosaunee (Iroquois Confederacy), the Conspiracy the &quot;Sons of Sosondowa&quot; are brought together by Hiwatha and the Great Peacemaker themselves to carry out the Great Law against cannibal witches and their cults. Probably lean to the earlier date interpretation, tying it to the 1142 solar eclipse.<br /> <br /> <b>Dante's Italy Geist: </b>Late medieval italy as the Holy Roman Empire and the Papacy wrestle for power. Ideally this setting will tie in Inferno updates for 2nd Edition, with a whole metaphysical plotline about the Underworld accessible from Italy's Autochthenous Depths are being corrupted by demons, making Sin-Eaters all the more important to save the dead.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Turn Mummy:</b> Update &quot;Infinite Macabre&quot; to 2nd Edition. The search for Alaru in the stars themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Near Future Demon:</b> Update &quot;Bleeding Edge&quot; to 2nd Edition. The hook for this setting is that the God Machine is maintaining multiple &quot;futures&quot; (well... presents) simultaneously, and the Unchained have the ability to move between them. So you have the &quot;total global surveillance state integrated directly into the infrastructure of the Machine itself&quot; future - you have the &quot;rival megacorps vie for power comodifying Pacts and Embeds&quot; future - you have the &quot;environmental catastrophe&quot; future - etc, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Terrible&quot; Russia Beast: </b>Ivan the Terrible serving the role of Apex, links the birth of this diverse empire through fear pretty well to Beast, with plenty of room for other supernatural weirdness for Beasts to be Kin to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T12:29:10-08:00","id":1041402,"title":"","content":"I'll reiterate my usual pitches of Ayutthaya Werewolf, and either First or Fourth Crusade middle east Werewolf. However, I'd also be tempted to fish through Ming Dynasty history for weird events that a good Werewolf chapter could hang off; or alternatively I'd want to go with 1800s Hong Kong Werewolf, specifically the bit where the British conflicted with the five Great Clans of the walled villages in the surrounding area.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr, alternatively, 10th Century Poland Werewolf - the Baptism of Poland in 966, the annihilation of the pagan faiths and the beginning of the Polish nation. Or maybe the later 1300s or 1400s with the wars with the Teutonic order.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr, fuckit, Vatican Werewolf during one of the particularly turbulent eras for the Papacy.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr Attila: Total Werewolf because, again, why not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T12:37:03-08:00","id":1041410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041402#post1041402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll reiterate my usual pitches of Ayutthaya Werewolf, and either First or Fourth Crusade middle east Werewolf. However, I'd also be tempted to fish through Ming Dynasty history for weird events that a good Werewolf chapter could hang off; or alternatively I'd want to go with 1800s Hong Kong Werewolf, specifically the bit where the British conflicted with the five Great Clans of the walled villages in the surrounding area.<br /> <br /> Or, alternatively, 10th Century Poland Werewolf - the Baptism of Poland in 966, the annihilation of the pagan faiths and the beginning of the Polish nation. Or maybe the later 1300s or 1400s with the wars with the Teutonic order.<br /> <br /> Or, fuckit, Vatican Werewolf during one of the particularly turbulent eras for the Papacy.<br /> <br /> Or Attila: Total Werewolf because, again, why not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want Ayutthaya Werewolf something fierce, but all of those would be awesome. Vatican Werewolf would be super interesting, especially since it is way out of where you would usually expect Werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T12:39:31-08:00","id":1041412,"title":"","content":"Heh, those all sound good. I don't know why people like Bau werewolf, it's utterly disassociated from its time period and is something you could pull off in modern day with a couple rites and gifts and the appropriate community.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041410#post1041410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want Ayutthaya Werewolf something fierce, but all of those would be awesome. Vatican Werewolf would be super interesting, especially since it is way out of where you would usually expect Werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something that should change, and these books seem like fine places to do it. Werewolves aren't all primitive barbarians, they aren't part of the wild or associated with nature. They live in cities and politic with everyone else just like vampires and mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T12:45:07-08:00","id":1041414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041412#post1041412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh, those all sound good. I don't know why people like Bau werewolf, it's utterly disassociated from its time period and is something you could pull off in modern day with a couple rites and gifts and the appropriate community.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I want to use it to make a distinct period showing the post-Sundering pre-Oath Werewolf world and the nature of the Oath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:13:48-08:00","id":1041507,"title":"","content":"Super super grim.<br /> <br /> But Irish Potato Famine. <br /> <br /> Massive death toll, well into the millions. So Geist, crossed over with overworked Uratha.<br /> <br /> Like I said, dark as all hell. But potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3192-baileyborough","name":"baileyborough","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T17:32:04-08:00","id":1041584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041339#post1041339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a few pitches, I'll add more later...<br /> <br /> <b>Qin Dynasty Vampire: </b>Covenants that rose of the Hundred Schools of Thought. The Legalist Covenant (which in addition to bureaucratic governance of vampires is also the culture's &quot;we are monsters who are supposed to keep humanity in line through fear&quot; faction) is beginning to enforce 'Shu' (the Masquerade) on the rest of the Kindred. The Confucian Covenant (feudal rule + serving as active &quot;ancestors&quot; with filial relationships with living family and necromantically with the passed) is fighting back HARD. Meanwhile a Taoist Covenant explores the mysteries of Blood Alchemy. If the chapter is expanded, it incorporates &quot;Immortals&quot; updates for 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> <b>Wolves of Bau (2nd Editon)</b>: Updated with the revelation of how (relatively) recent the Sundering was, this setting is represented as being before/during the Oaths of the Moon. The rulership of Bau is a failed attempt for the Uratha to carve out a place for themselves in the world before turning instead to readopting Father Wolf's cause. The Oaths of the Moon are presented as a Rite that exists in the setting, readopting the lost auspices at the cost of losing the special advantages of the Bau setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd absolutelly love both of those settings. Years ago, I began to write a Chinese setting for Requiem (never went beyond first drafts), and I also created covenants based on the different schols of thought of ancient chinese philosophy.<br /> <br /> My thoughts about Dark Eras 2:<br /> <br /> 1) I'd love it to be so successful that Onyx Path finally decides to write some Dark Eras gamelines, although limited, as WoD Dark Ages, Sorcerers Crusade, Wild West... I loved Requiem for Rome, but it was too short. Or at least, although they were oneshots, that each gameline, in the curse of one or two years, ahd at least an historical setting book.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2) As someone said before, I think there should be Eras that are important for each setting:<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire: </b>The main historical setting was The Camarilla, but that was done with Requiem for Rome. So, may be a Rome setting during the Stryx Rules, during Roman Monarchy, that would end with the Julius Senex revolt and the stablish the Camarilla. It would be a nive way to update RfR rules (benefits of the Wings and Julii weakness) without making just an update to 2nd Edition of RfR, but offering something new. Another possibility could be a settin centered in the barbarian kingdoms after the Fall of Rome, centered on the transition from Camarilla to the birth of the Invictus.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf: </b>A setting after the Fall of Urfarah but before/during the birth of the Tribes. Glamourweaver idea of the City of Bau is perfect (I liked it a lot but it was soooooo short), so I wont expand on it. Other possibilities could be the coming of the Idigam and the Brethens War from 1st Edition Corebook. But Id really offer my firstborn for a Sumerian werewolf setting.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage:</b> Tha Nameless War that ended woth the birth of the Free Council. Its the most important event from mage in last centuries, and it would offer an interesting twist as showing protolibertines and Diamond mages as enemies in an open war. Another possibility could be a Roman setting that showed the institutionalization of the Darshanas in full Orders.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter:</b> I think there are three settings linked to important moments on Hunter history: Ancient Mesopotamia with the Nibiru and Ancient Rome with the Aves Minerva. Another setting could be the U.S. Independence war, with the Cheasnut Street Compact from Philadelphia, but may be it would too much similar to Dobting Souls.<br /> <br /> <b>Geist: </b>I think that some historical moments with a very hig death toll could be interesting: The Black Death (or the Justinian's Plague), the Conquest of Americas, First World War (and the Spanish Flu) or Second World War.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy:</b> All the Sothic Circles have been done, so I'd suggest may be an Irem Dark Era, may be crossover with Mage around the Irem's war against the Kir-En-Gi dark mages of Kish.<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean, Changeling, Demon and Beast: </b>I don't remember any so important history moment about first two and I havent read the other two.<br /> <br /> Later, Il'l continue with other settings Id like, although they are not as decisive moments of the history of the splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 01-31-2017, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T18:06:40-08:00","id":1041602,"title":"","content":"A Dark Era during Irem would undermine the themes of the game like Memory and the fact that you don't get to remember your entire mortal life unless you have a very high score in that trait.<br /> <br /> Also, you wouldn't be a mummy yet anyway lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T18:17:16-08:00","id":1041606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041602#post1041602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Dark Era during Irem would undermine the themes of the game like Memory and the fact that you don't get to remember your entire mortal life unless you have a very high score in that trait.<br /> <br /> Also, you wouldn't be a mummy yet anyway lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. While it would be cool, I'd rather that Irem were explored through Mummy's own books. A Dark Era set then could be too disruptive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T20:16:05-08:00","id":1041657,"title":"","content":"Having too much of a canonical Irem spoils the fun anyway, and half the point of Mummy is mucking about across the ages of real history: I don't come to Mummy for a mortals game in a magical era that doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> You wanna do a Mummy Dark Era, get weird with it and take us to Asia or South America. Let it be somewhere Irem never directly touched, to really highlight how adrift the Arisen are and so I can make my kung fu Deceived canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T20:33:08-08:00","id":1041666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041657#post1041657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You wanna do a Mummy Dark Era, get weird with it and take us to Asia or South America.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't there a whole book about Mummy in Rio de Janeiro? Yeah the core book says they were all over South and Central America long before the Europeans arrived.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T21:13:27-08:00","id":1041672,"title":"","content":"I have an idea for an Inca Empire Mummy Era that specifically focuses on the Twice-Risen surging (the Incans make a human sacrifice based on visions from the gods, and that body arises divine - in truth one of the Arisen who had lost their original bodies now merged into the new persona)... but I worry it would be too &quot;Inca religion is a sham covering a proto-Egyptian religion&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T22:05:10-08:00","id":1041686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041672#post1041672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an idea for an Inca Empire Mummy Era that specifically focuses on the Twice-Risen surging (the Incans make a human sacrifice based on visions from the gods, and that body arises divine - in truth one of the Arisen who had lost their original bodies now merged into the new persona)... but I worry it would be too &quot;Inca religion is a sham covering a proto-Egyptian religion&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd make for a pretty interesting setting, particularly since odds are more of said Mummies would rise as Shuankhsen than as Arisen.<br /> <br /> I feel like the concern about being disrespectful towards Incan religion can be ameliorated pretty easily. Cults are doing it, not the central Incan religion. That's the default approach for all of Mummy to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T22:06:50-08:00","id":1041687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041657#post1041657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having too much of a canonical Irem spoils the fun anyway, and half the point of Mummy is mucking about across the ages of real history: I don't come to Mummy for a mortals game in a magical era that doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> You wanna do a Mummy Dark Era, get weird with it and take us to Asia or South America. Let it be somewhere Irem never directly touched, to really highlight how adrift the Arisen are and so I can make my kung fu Deceived canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't a Kung Fu Deceived literally part of the Book of the Deceived's intro fiction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T01:16:39-08:00","id":1041733,"title":"","content":"More Dark Era settings in Asia:<br /> <br /> <b>Akbar the Great and the Mughal Empire</b><br /> 1556. For half a century, a tenuous peace persists in India under one the Mughals' most visionary rulers. Akbar's court is filled with artists, scientists, and holy men. In contrast to the Western Diamond Precept, Mughal Awakened refine the Darshanas to their own accord. The Jnanashakti subtly guide the emperor as he fuses elements of Islam, Hinduism, Zoroastrianism, and Christianity into a syncretic and controversial new religion. In search of righteous warfare, the Vajrastra join Akbar's mansabdari ranks. With the exotic kingdoms of India awaiting conquest, they will soon have their fill. <br /> <br /> <b>The Taiping Rebellion</b><br /> 1850. The Middle Kingdom is thrown into civil war when an apocalyptic religious sect revolts against the Qing. As Hong Xiuquan - a man who claims to be the younger brother of Jesus Christ - rallies half a million followers to create a new heaven on earth, so too do the solitary Demons of Nanjing jealously guard their long-denied freedoms. Yet nothing lasts forever. Every day, the Taiping Kingdom's enemies grow in number and power. Will the Unchained stay, or flee once again?<br /> <br /> <b>Japanese Conquest of Southeast Asia</b><br /> 1941. Manila, Singapura, Batavia, Saigon, and Rangoon. Follow the secret networks of Kindred across Southeast Asia as their cities fall before the Empire of Japan. Will the Covenants survive the grand ambitions of the so-called 'Asian Co-Prosperity Sphere', or will vampire-kind burn along with their fiefdoms? As a bonus, this chapter will provide various new Bloodlines unique to the local cultures such as the Aswang, Langsuir, Pontianak, Riri Yaka and Jiangshi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T03:12:28-08:00","id":1041754,"title":"","content":"while I do enjoy having non-Western Eras, I'm also very interested in new Western ones (maybe because I'm not European/American, who knows?). Anyway, one Era I would really like to see is a Second Punic War Demon/Hunter Crossover (or maybe Mummy/Demon, or Demon/Inferno. There are many ways to work it out). A Promethean Bar Kokhba Revolt could also be interesting to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T03:19:10-08:00","id":1041755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041657#post1041657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You wanna do a Mummy Dark Era, get weird with it and take us to Asia or South America. Let it be somewhere Irem never directly touched, to really highlight how adrift the Arisen are and so I can make my kung fu Deceived canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the time I really wanted my expansion to go to Ruins of Empire and I know another backer picked it for their expanded Era <i>and</i> I'm <b>very</b> happy with the Cleopatra chapter expansion we got to do in light of the Ruins of Empire additions, BUT in hindsight, had I not known any of those things would happen, I like to imagine my initial expansion going to a Skinchangers/Mummy Aztec crossover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041672#post1041672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an idea for an Inca Empire Mummy Era that specifically focuses on the Twice-Risen surging (the Incans make a human sacrifice based on visions from the gods, and that body arises divine - in truth one of the Arisen who had lost their original bodies now merged into the new persona)... but I worry it would be too &quot;Inca religion is a sham covering a proto-Egyptian religion&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like we all jumped on that during the polls, too, so part of me is wondering why the developers didn't find it interesting. I'm still glad they went with Cleopatra because that's pretty iconic, and it turned out to be an interesting chapter as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T05:15:58-08:00","id":1041767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041328#post1041328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone will probably point out that a writer has already said otherwise, but I imagine if we're ever going to get a kitchen sink setting, it would be in the Crossover Book, which would show examples of said crossover in said kitchen sink setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall hearing anything like that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But I could see it beng something they wouldn't want to tackle unless they Crossover Chronicle comes out first. I wouldn't mind such an era, though (Renaissance Italy would be my go-to for it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041584#post1041584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Geist: </b>I think that some historical moments with a very hig death toll could be interesting: The Black Death (or the Justinian's Plague), the Conquest of Americas, First World War (and the Spanish Flu) or Second World War.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're already getting the Black Death in the Companion (for Geist and Vampire). Rather than the Conquest of the Americas, I'd rather see the Triple Alliance: the <i>beginning</i> of the Aztec empire rather than its end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Promethean, Changeling, Demon and Beast: </b>I don't remember any so important history moment about first two and I havent read the other two. </div> </div> </div>The eras I know of for Promethean feature giant parallels of the Wasteland and Disquiet. One parallelling the Pilgrimmage might be interesting: ie, one where there is a big systematic change overtaking society. The early Soviet Union perhaps (to emphasise a planned and deliberate transformation). Or the spread of Buddhism in Central Asia (to emphasise a transformation championing enlightenment).<br /> <br /> Beast... it's a facet of the setting that Heroes were originally supposed to distill wisdom from their confrontations with Beasts and pass it on to the populace at large. But the mental landscape of humanity has become too noisy, and Heroes don't really do this any more. An era where Heroes still work as they're &quot;supposed to&quot; - where they're both enemies of Beasts, but also kind of their partners, would be interesting.<br /> Or else, the time of the Brothers Grimm - they might be called fairy stories, but Beasts reflect the monsters in those tales more than changelings do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041755#post1041755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like we all jumped on that during the polls, too, so part of me is wondering why the developers didn't find it interesting. I'm still glad they went with Cleopatra because that's pretty iconic, and it turned out to be an interesting chapter as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because of how contentious the subject of non-Iremite mummies gets. People who don't care about those tend to advance twice-risen and/or lost memories as a solution for people who want them - whereas to people who <i>do</i> see the lack of them as a problem, those suggestions tend to come across as making it even worse - and there are people who dislike the idea of non-Iremite mummies enough that they'd reject any attempt to cater to the idea or include suggestions on representing them. Either way, I can see the writers preferring to go for an era that'd cause fewer arguments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T05:55:30-08:00","id":1041778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041767#post1041767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I<br /> I think we're already getting the Black Death in the Companion (for Geist and Vampire). Rather than the Conquest of the Americas, I'd rather see the Triple Alliance: the <i>beginning</i> of the Aztec empire rather than its end.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Black Death Era is Promethean/Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T06:17:39-08:00","id":1041785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041754#post1041754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">while I do enjoy having non-Western Eras, I'm also very interested in new Western ones (maybe because I'm not European/American, who knows?). Anyway, one Era I would really like to see is a Second Punic War Demon/Hunter Crossover (or maybe Mummy/Demon, or Demon/Inferno. There are many ways to work it out). A Promethean Bar Kokhba Revolt could also be interesting to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo, as Yet Another Pitch from me: I'd love to do Industrial Revolution Werewolf in Europe, with the Uratha struggling to cope with the tidal wave of new spirit courts and colossally powerful spirit nobles birthed from the industrialisation taking place, the pollution and machinery masking the scuttling presence of a huge boom in the power of the Beshilu, and the social conflicts of the human population through whom this new era is being birthed. Iron Masters trying to chain massive industry spirit-gods into obeisance, a grand Rat Host plan to pull hellish, interstitial-place Other Cities into the world and establish a Plague Dominion, bizarre Claimed-machinery masterminds spreading their influence with every piece of track laid down for the trains that serve as their limbs and minds, human spiritualists' interference threatening the People, and the way everything fed into the demand for more raw materials, for the spreading of power, for the grasping reach of empires bourne up upon the back of industry's march.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T06:30:59-08:00","id":1041788,"title":"","content":"I'd also love to see the Industrial Revolution in another Dark Eras book, but rather than just Werewolf, I'd want it to be a mega chapter for an everyday crossover setting. Between Vampire, Mage, Demon and the rest, I think each would have their own interesting problems and chances coming about during the period. (Like the great refusal as long as I'm not screwing up memory wise for the timeline.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T07:23:40-08:00","id":1041814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041402#post1041402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll reiterate my usual pitches of Ayutthaya Werewolf, and either First or Fourth Crusade middle east Werewolf. However, I'd also be tempted to fish through Ming Dynasty history for weird events that a good Werewolf chapter could hang off; or alternatively I'd want to go with 1800s Hong Kong Werewolf, specifically the bit where the British conflicted with the five Great Clans of the walled villages in the surrounding area.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr, alternatively, 10th Century Poland Werewolf - the Baptism of Poland in 966, the annihilation of the pagan faiths and the beginning of the Polish nation. Or maybe the later 1300s or 1400s with the wars with the Teutonic order.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr, fuckit, Vatican Werewolf during one of the particularly turbulent eras for the Papacy.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr Attila: Total Werewolf because, again, why not.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041785#post1041785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSo, as Yet Another Pitch from me: I'd love to do Industrial Revolution Werewolf in Europe, with the Uratha struggling to cope with the tidal wave of new spirit courts and colossally powerful spirit nobles birthed from the industrialisation taking place, the pollution and machinery masking the scuttling presence of a huge boom in the power of the Beshilu, and the social conflicts of the human population through whom this new era is being birthed. Iron Masters trying to chain massive industry spirit-gods into obeisance, a grand Rat Host plan to pull hellish, interstitial-place Other Cities into the world and establish a Plague Dominion, bizarre Claimed-machinery masterminds spreading their influence with every piece of track laid down for the trains that serve as their limbs and minds, human spiritualists' interference threatening the People, and the way everything fed into the demand for more raw materials, for the spreading of power, for the grasping reach of empires bourne up upon the back of industry's march.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1757\" data-vbnamecard=\"1757\">Acrozatarim</a>, you sound like this:<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://cdn.meme.am/cache/instances/folder737/500x/75234737.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> But I'm totally buying this, as Werewolf is a bit 'less loved' main gameline. Baptism of Poland would be extremly interesting ( we got our own 'Vikings equivalents' in those times ) and as Iron Masters guy, I'm for Industrial Revolution. I'm also would crossover it with at least Mage and it's Nameless War of that time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Vatican Werewolf sounds so 'baaad'... ( in a good way! ) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:13:26-08:00","id":1041834,"title":"","content":"I don't want to do the Nameless War / Great Refusal in a Dark Era. The format's too short for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:29:17-08:00","id":1041840,"title":"","content":"It was global, right? Seems like its own book would be more appropriate. It would be interesting to see some of the more prominent Nameless Orders. The whole 'lost organizations' thing is one of the coolest parts of second edition, starting from way back in Blood &amp; Smoke's lost clans and lost covenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:47:13-08:00","id":1041851,"title":"","content":"Poo, I wanted an era that was Persia in the Nameless War, specifically to find out more about Razi. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041840#post1041840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was global, right? Seems like its own book would be more appropriate. It would be interesting to see some of the more prominent Nameless Orders. The whole 'lost organizations' thing is one of the coolest parts of second edition, starting from way back in Blood &amp; Smoke's lost clans and lost covenants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I really would like to see some Nameless Orders fleshed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:59:48-08:00","id":1041859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041785#post1041785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bSo, as Yet Another Pitch from me: I'd love to do Industrial Revolution Werewolf in Europe, with the Uratha struggling to cope with the tidal wave of new spirit courts and colossally powerful spirit nobles birthed from the industrialisation taking place, the pollution and machinery masking the scuttling presence of a huge boom in the power of the Beshilu, and the social conflicts of the human population through whom this new era is being birthed. Iron Masters trying to chain massive industry spirit-gods into obeisance, a grand Rat Host plan to pull hellish, interstitial-place Other Cities into the world and establish a Plague Dominion, bizarre Claimed-machinery masterminds spreading their influence with every piece of track laid down for the trains that serve as their limbs and minds, human spiritualists' interference threatening the People, and the way everything fed into the demand for more raw materials, for the spreading of power, for the grasping reach of empires bourne up upon the back of industry's march.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's sounds excellent. It would be even better as Demon and/or Mage crossover.<br /> <br /> The Industrial Revolution's impact on the God Machine must have been colossal.<br /> <br /> The Mysteries birthed by the Industrial Revolution, and new and novel applications of the Arcana, would also be perfect for Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:37:22-08:00","id":1041875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041834#post1041834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to do the Nameless War / Great Refusal in a Dark Era. The format's too short for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the announcement of the chapter on Nameless War in the <b>Tome of Pentacle</b>? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:39:37-08:00","id":1041876,"title":"","content":"Why would &quot;the format's too short for it&quot; be an announcement of an even shorter section?<br /> <br /> No, it's not an announcement of anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:42:41-08:00","id":1041877,"title":"","content":"@DaveB well then I hope you get enough traction for a full Nameless War/Great Refusal book ala the Requiem for Rome pair. I for one would buy it in an instant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:54:34-08:00","id":1041887,"title":"","content":"I really hope Vampire comes out strong, it didn't get enough love during the first Dark Eras, even though Requiem for Regina was one of the better ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:29:27-08:00","id":1041904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041834#post1041834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to do the Nameless War / Great Refusal in a Dark Era. The format's too short for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As a single era meant to cover the whole century all over the globe, yeah I can definietly see that. Would it be plausible though to have an important snippet of it in an era though? Like see it breaking out in a Revolutionary France setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:37:39-08:00","id":1041908,"title":"","content":"I'm actually going to be a bit boring here: I want rise of the HRE in Europe (for practically anyone). The traditional middle ages at their height. The reason being that... Well. It's the middle ages.<br /> I'm getting a bit of a feeling that some of the eras are way too... I don't know how to put it... Niche?<br /> I'd like something a bit broader. Something a bit more well known.<br /> <br /> Also, of course, I am going to second Chris' Industrial Revolution.<br /> <br /> And, honestly, anywhere that gives us a write-up of a whole new vampire covenant. Preferably an Arabian or Persian one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:41:27-08:00","id":1041911,"title":"","content":"I thought, since Requiem for Rome, that they tried to avoid traditional 'Dark Ages' because that was classic's thing. But Viking werewolf certainly broached on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-01-2017, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:47:56-08:00","id":1041915,"title":"","content":"More abstractly, I want settings that add new Covenants to Vampire, new Nameless Orders to Mage, more Courts to Changeling, and possibly new philosophies outside of the lessons thing for Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T11:01:02-08:00","id":1041924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041908#post1041908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually going to be a bit boring here: I want rise of the HRE in Europe (for practically anyone). The traditional middle ages at their height. The reason being that... Well. It's the middle ages..</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides the Dante's Italy one I mentioned, my main idea or a medieval Europe setting was to do a Hunter/Demon crossover in Cathar France. The Bon Hommes are a Gnostic Compact that struggles against the Demiurge of the Material World (God Machine), The Sacred Order of the Knights of Saint George (Conspiracy, and a secret division of the Templars) are not solely Mage-focused yet, and fight against any unholy beings who would defy the order of creation and bring down divine wrath from outside of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T11:08:28-08:00","id":1041929,"title":"","content":"Have I already talked about my Mythic Greek Beast/Changeling crossover, where Beasts are self-appointed Furies who believe they act on behalf of the Olympian gods they've never seen but don't know how to handle the Lost, who are touched by the &quot;divine&quot; and scarred by the experience?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T12:01:27-08:00","id":1041944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041814#post1041814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1757\" data-vbnamecard=\"1757\">Acrozatarim</a>, you sound like this:<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, I have a few ideas for Mage and Vampire ones too, but Werewolf is where I'm most confident in how I'd match the themes and events together.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T12:19:28-08:00","id":1041955,"title":"","content":"Can we hear some of your vampire ideas?<br /> <br /> Also do you have any werewolf + vampire ideas for Eras? I find the double-up concept interesting but it seems harder to pull off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:47:19-08:00","id":1042006,"title":"","content":"I'd love to do something for Vampire in India. Not sure exactly when, but I think I'd want to aim at a period of major decline for a ruling power. Have all sorts of fun stuff running around; rakshasa, vetala, etc.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, a bit of a non-standard one: Book of Highways and Kingdoms Vampire, ie 11th Century north and central Africa. I'd love to see it done in an almost travelogue style touching on a series of vampire polities and cultures, from regular Kindred to weirder stuff like areas where the Adze of Ghanan folklore are a dominant subspecies. Have an Al-Bakri-esque figure writing about the various areas from their distant viewpoint, then with a description of what it's really like from a local point of view, rules for key elements, etc. You could get an amazing overview of how the Kindred had adapted in some really interesting cultures and nations of the time.<br /> <br /> For Vampire &amp; Werewolf, I'd want to do a Mongol expansion era; either the reign of Genghis, or a more specific area a few generations down the line like early Yuan China. Werewolf is obvious, but the reason for Vampire is because, well... think about it. Pre-expansion, what does it mean to be a vampire in the Land of the Eternal Blue Sky? What sort of vampire societies and oddities would form in those circumstances? And then, following their expansion, how do the Kindred societies carried into contact with the existing vampiric populations of subjugated areas cope? Do they adapt and become rulers, or do they become ruled in turn? How are they forced to change to survive, and what changes do they force on the Kindred in the lands conquered and ruled by the Mongols?<br /> <br /> \u200bAnother Vampire/Werewolf crossover I'd want is Beast of Gevaudan France. There's already some groundwork laid in the Werewolf 2e corebook about Gevaudan, and it'd be an intriguing scenario to have Uratha and French vampires all caught up scheming, allying, fighting and backstabbing one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:03:16-08:00","id":1042018,"title":"","content":"I've been trying to put together a pitch for 1960s Hunter (or possibly Hunter/Changeling) and the words just aren't coming to me.<br /> <br /> I know it's a good idea, damn it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T18:38:03-08:00","id":1042155,"title":"","content":"The thread on the Mist-Blinded has reminded me... I'd to see some more Proximi and other demisplats in some Eras. Ghoul families would en another good addition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T18:39:25-08:00","id":1042156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1042006#post1042006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to do something for Vampire in India. Not sure exactly when, but I think I'd want to aim at a period of major decline for a ruling power. Have all sorts of fun stuff running around; rakshasa, vetala, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat, the bloodline books for vampire started to lean heavily towards the East, which I thought was a trend it was going to stick with but didn't, there's a lot of cool stuff that was never expanded on. Plus obviously a huge area with a long past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bAlso, a bit of a non-standard one: Book of Highways and Kingdoms Vampire, ie 11th Century north and central Africa. I'd love to see it done in an almost travelogue style touching on a series of vampire polities and cultures, from regular Kindred to weirder stuff like areas where the Adze of Ghanan folklore are a dominant subspecies. Have an Al-Bakri-esque figure writing about the various areas from their distant viewpoint, then with a description of what it's really like from a local point of view, rules for key elements, etc. You could get an amazing overview of how the Kindred had adapted in some really interesting cultures and nations of the time.<br /> <br /> For Vampire &amp; Werewolf, I'd want to do a Mongol expansion era; either the reign of Genghis, or a more specific area a few generations down the line like early Yuan China. Werewolf is obvious, but the reason for Vampire is because, well... think about it. Pre-expansion, what does it mean to be a vampire in the Land of the Eternal Blue Sky? What sort of vampire societies and oddities would form in those circumstances? And then, following their expansion, how do the Kindred societies carried into contact with the existing vampiric populations of subjugated areas cope? Do they adapt and become rulers, or do they become ruled in turn? How are they forced to change to survive, and what changes do they force on the Kindred in the lands conquered and ruled by the Mongols? </div> </div> </div>People are always asking for more Asian and African eras, and if your Likes are anything it seems like you've got some good ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bAnother Vampire/Werewolf crossover I'd want is Beast of Gevaudan France. There's already some groundwork laid in the Werewolf 2e corebook about Gevaudan, and it'd be an intriguing scenario to have Uratha and French vampires all caught up scheming, allying, fighting and backstabbing one another. </div> </div> </div>That's the quicksilver children and possibly an idigam there, right? Bickering and power plays among the two creatures of the night would be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T03:33:50-08:00","id":1042327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041778#post1041778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Black Death Era is Promethean/Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Even so, it makes it less likely we'll be seeing the era again for anything else, which is a shame, because I agree the plague would suit Geist pretty well. Maybe the London 1603 outbreak instead - it's the same disease, it's the year Elizabeth I dies, Londerners in general kept well informed of how many people died of what (which is an interesting element for Geist, I think), and krewe culture could be tied in with theatre culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T04:55:46-08:00","id":1042350,"title":"","content":"I think I'll offer up Cuban Revolution.<br /> <br /> Guerrilla bands fighting capitalist imperials for their destiny in the jungles of the Caribbean. Hell yes. Mummies rise up to wreak havoc on the old guard while werewolves ally with spirits of revolution, or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T05:03:03-08:00","id":1042353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1042350#post1042350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'll offer up Cuban Revolution.<br /> <br /> Guerrilla bands fighting capitalist imperials for their destiny in the jungles of the Caribbean. Hell yes. Mummies rise up to wreak havoc on the old guard while werewolves ally with spirits of revolution, or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just seeing this Carthian and Free Council alliance to overthrow 'old regime' of they own societies!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T08:09:08-08:00","id":1042421,"title":"","content":"I like the Cuban Revolution idea, big fan of the Caribbean and for other reasons.<br /> <br /> Don't know how popular it would be, though, Haiti after Papa Doc was up for votes too and people really seemed to want to avoid it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T19:26:28-08:00","id":1042750,"title":"","content":"Ok, so a few crossover pitches<br /> <br /> Hunter/Mummy - Book of Judges (Israelite Shoftim defend their land from dark gods and their cults, while those cults are fleeing Akhenaten back in Egypt)<br /> <br /> Mage/Changeling - Golden Age of Islam (1001 Nights!)<br /> <br /> Hunter/Demon - Cathar France (Gnostic Compact struggles against the Demiurge, while the Templar Knights of St George hunt those who would subvert natural law and corrupt the faithful)<br /> <br /> Promethean/Demon - Mansa Musa Pilgrimage (the pilgrimage of course works great for Prometheans, and the new infrastructure linking the Mali Empire to the greater Muslim world in the east has great DtD potential; the hook is conflicting signs from Angels and Qashmallim, leaning into the mystery of the God Machine and the Principle)<br /> <br /> Mage/Geist - Golden Age of Piracy (would also work to swap either out for Demon, but Geist was the possible era last time, and Mage has a hook story hook in this era as the Silver Ladder and the Seers of the Throne allied against the Nassau Nameless - my idea is that this could create a non-aggression relationship that underlies a Libertine alliance with dissastisfied Diamond Mages almost a century later in the French Revolution)<br /> <br /> Mage/Beast - French Revolution (I know the original proposed era would have been Mage/Mummy, but as we're getting Mage/Mummy with the Mutapa Empire, I thought this might work better as something different. The outbreak of the Nameless War, paired with rotating Apexes struggling to define the Paris Hive. It's literally called &quot;the Terror&quot; for a reason)<br /> <br /> Vampire/Hunter - Pre-Mutiny India (chance to update and substantially expand on the caste Bloodlines of India, with the thuggee hook for Hunters that was offered as one of the possible eras last time)<br /> <br /> Werewolf/Geist - Great War (the Horsemen themselves stalk the earth as war, famine, influenza rage; soldiers touch death and are reborn in the trenches while the Uratha stalk new more and more horrific spirits of slaughter and industrialized devastation)<br /> <br /> Vampire/Beast - Jazz Age (intrigue and beauty of the Harlem Renaissance set against the era of the greatest post-Civil War racial violence in American History, with a touch of Lovecraft)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T22:43:09-08:00","id":1042824,"title":"","content":"To borrow your format, then:<br /> <br /> Werewolf - Meiji Japan (the Forsaken are bound to old traditions as foreign modernity intrudes; will they die off with the turning of the age like the samurai and the Japanese wolf [which poetically goes extinct around this time] or kill the old Japan like they once killed Father Wolf when he grew weak?)<br /> <br /> Hunter/Changeling, possibly Deviant - 1960s America (New Age cults and Slashers [who may well become 'Mansons' by the end of the decade] keep the dubiously-moral organizations of the time hunting while people return from psychedelic jungles to a rapidly-changing homeland that's on the brink of an unpleasant psychic awakening; an excuse to make Hotel Mascaron canon)<br /> <br /> Changeling/Beast - Mythic Greece (the Begotten are self-appointed Furies who believe the gods have sent them to punish hubris but have their credibility threatened by the Lost who are heirs to the divine punishments of Arachne and Medusa)<br /> <br /> Vampire/Demon - 1930s Shanghai (the Pearl of the Orient sees her neon-drenched streets occupied by Imperial Japanese and her back alleys flood with White Russian mobsters, local crime bosses, Nazi spies, and wealthy fools from the West looking for an exotic good time; espionage and murder are the name of the game, but there's older and greater things here than the newest mortal nations)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T23:06:04-08:00","id":1042831,"title":"","content":"Everything from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> last posts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T23:27:41-08:00","id":1042841,"title":"","content":"Chicago World's Fair - ALL! (the intrigue of Requiem in the White City is obvious; you also can tie Deviant directly into the eugenics age, Mages dabble in such fields themselves as the modern tech loving Namess draw closer with the Seers as the Nameless War sputters and the Great Refusal nears, Prometheans are drawn in the Current Wars, Demons struggle to find new ways to hide as the God Machine's infrastructure now spans the continent more overtly than ever, one of history's greatest Slashers does his work in the fair's shadows.... etc etc)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T23:30:23-08:00","id":1042843,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to think of just which gamelines fit best for Victorian Hong Kong and the answer seems to be literally all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T00:06:45-08:00","id":1042848,"title":"","content":"Era we've seen before, but I have a ton of notes for &quot;Vigil For Rome&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T01:12:50-08:00","id":1042860,"title":"","content":"Having thought about this the area that I want to know more about would be Vampires and the move to the new world. This is mostly for the practical side of it (getting over there and getting set up) but I'm one of those people who likes physical books so there's a good chance it would be some time before I buy a copy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T01:20:10-08:00","id":1042861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1042860#post1042860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having thought about this the area that I want to know more about would be Vampires and the move to the new world. This is mostly for the practical side of it (getting over there and getting set up) but I'm one of those people who likes physical books so there's a good chance it would be some time before I buy a copy.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Doubting Souls</i> Era touched on this briefly, but I'm be more than willing to see this great Age of Exploration and all those Old World monsters founding that they are <i>not</i> first to prey on humanity in wilderness parts of world. My Mysterium, Iron Masters and Ordo Dracul researchers would be especially interested in this. Waiting to see those exotic Nameless Orders that mage would try to subdue with their 'Atlantean Rethorics'. Especially as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1041771-dark-eras-cheiron-group-acheron-shipping-trading-guild-invented-black-death\">Cherion Group is rumored to set sails earlier to New World than rest of humanity</a>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-03-2017, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T03:11:54-08:00","id":1042873,"title":"","content":"Oh, another Vampire/Werewolf idea that's been stewing in my mind: Medici Florentine. Werewolf's packs/gangs conflict maps very well onto the political conflicts of the time as you escalate up the scale, from rival street gangs to feuding noble families and banker clans to rival city-states to the chaotic mess of various rival Popes, etc etc. It's a time of change for the human cultures involved, artistically and politically and governmentally and spiritually; all rich stuff to play off with Werewolf. Vampire fits right in with all that for obvious reasons too. I'd pick a specific event or social current and make it a flashpoint for both types of supernatural. Maybe add some high weirdness - something supernatural and odd going on specifically at this very time that both are struggling to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T07:57:32-08:00","id":1042948,"title":"","content":"I've said it before, and I'll say it again. I'd like to see the Dancing Plague of 1518 (or really, any outbreak of dancing mania) covered in the Chronicles of Darkness. I don't particularly care about which line would get it. Changeling seems like it would be good for the Pied Piper similarities. Hunter would be good for simply having some weirdness to investigate. Hell, even it being the result of Mummy cultist activities could be possible. I see a lot of possibilities with that kind of a setting, and it seems a shame not to do something with it..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T08:18:54-08:00","id":1042960,"title":"","content":"Really, if we get French Revolution, I'm hoping that it gets a 10k expansion so that it can be Mage/Mummy/Beast. The Revolution is thematically on point for Beast, but historically it is a bit effing deal for Mage and Mummy. Mage sees conflict for the Seers of the Throne and the Silver Ladder, while for Mummy, it is the biggest rejection of the culture of Irem to date. I'd love to see Beast take on it, but I feel it is too historically important to Mummy and Mage to pass it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:09:03-08:00","id":1043110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1042848#post1042848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Era we've seen before, but I have a ton of notes for &amp;quot;Vigil For Rome&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I would pay an inordinate amount of money for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T19:19:41-08:00","id":1043312,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see something with one of the Muslim kingdoms in Iberia, ideally one of the earlier ones and centered around Vampire; you got all the fun of court politics and a religion-heavy society, but from a direction the average reader isn't familiar with. It would be a chance to see some new Covenants (you could get Muslim and Jewish groups in here, plus maybe a declining Gothic group as well) beyond the pretty lazy reskins that were in <i>Ancient Mysteries</i> (which I loved, but come on; &quot;just rename the Lance and Circle and call it a day&quot; really doesn't do it justice), some fun new Bloodlines, and a chance to see formerly-Roman Kindred that fled West instead of East.<br /> <br /> You could even tack a Fall of Granada appendix onto it as a stretch goal in the same way that Requiem for Rome did for Byzantium and do vignettes where the characters or their childer react to the Reconquista and die, convert, or flee into North Africa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T19:24:09-08:00","id":1043315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1043312#post1043312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see something with one of the Muslim kingdoms in Iberia, ideally one of the earlier ones and centered around Vampire; you got all the fun of court politics and a religion-heavy society, but from a direction the average reader isn't familiar with. It would be a chance to see some new Covenants (you could get Muslim and Jewish groups in here, plus maybe a declining Gothic group as well) beyond the pretty lazy reskins that were in <i>Ancient Mysteries</i> (which I loved, but come on; &quot;just rename the Lance and Circle and call it a day&quot; really doesn't do it justice), some fun new Bloodlines, and a chance to see formerly-Roman Kindred that fled West instead of East.<br /> <br /> You could even tack a Fall of Granada appendix onto it as a stretch goal in the same way that Requiem for Rome did for Byzantium and do vignettes where the characters or their childer react to the Reconquista and die, convert, or flee into North Africa.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to see a Cordoba Umayyad or Emirate of Sicily based era for anyone. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T19:28:53-08:00","id":1043316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1043315#post1043315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would love to see a Cordoba Umayyad or Emirate of Sicily based era for anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. You can't tell me Cordoba isn't a hotbed of intrigue that the Kindred would fit right into.<br /> <br /> And I'm sure the local Hunters are really interesting! You might even have pesky Christians sneaking in from Asturias to the north.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T20:00:19-08:00","id":1043328,"title":"","content":"Beast in Tokyo during the panic surrounding the monster with 21 faces case and the following Oronamin C (the method used the by the poisoner fitting Beast's teaching lessons through fear bit rather well) poisonings in 1984-85, two of the most famous unsolved crimes in Japanese history and theyt did more than anything else, made the Japanese afraid of crime in a way that they hadn't been for years, seems right up Beast's ally.<br /> <br /> I can also think of how post soviet Eastern Europe in the 90s fits the themes of several game lines","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T20:48:48-08:00","id":1043350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1043312#post1043312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see something with one of the Muslim kingdoms in Iberia, ideally one of the earlier ones and centered around Vampire; you got all the fun of court politics and a religion-heavy society, but from a direction the average reader isn't familiar with. It would be a chance to see some new Covenants (you could get Muslim and Jewish groups in here, plus maybe a declining Gothic group as well) beyond the pretty lazy reskins that were in <i>Ancient Mysteries</i> (which I loved, but come on; &quot;just rename the Lance and Circle and call it a day&quot; really doesn't do it justice), some fun new Bloodlines, and a chance to see formerly-Roman Kindred that fled West instead of East.<br /> <br /> You could even tack a Fall of Granada appendix onto it as a stretch goal in the same way that Requiem for Rome did for Byzantium and do vignettes where the characters or their childer react to the Reconquista and die, convert, or flee into North Africa.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd also love an al-Andalus setting. Although I had thought more a Mage Setting, showig the differences between &quot;christian&quot; and &quot;muslim&quot; versions of the Orders, with Cordoba as one of the greatest Athenaeain and magic centers of knowledge in the world, atracting mages of both East and West, Vampire would be my second option for that setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T21:51:07-08:00","id":1043380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1043350#post1043350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also love an al-Andalus setting. Although I had thought more a Mage Setting, showig the differences between &quot;christian&quot; and &quot;muslim&quot; versions of the Orders, with Cordoba as one of the greatest Athenaeain and magic centers of knowledge in the world, atracting mages of both East and West, Vampire would be my second option for that setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm itching for more Vampire settings in general, but Vampire/Mage could be a really fun crossover, especially anywhere that buried elders and buried Mysteries could overlap.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And now I'm wondering how you might overlap Atlantis myths with Ubar or Irem, with the obvious Mummy tie-in there...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 02-04-2017, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T22:53:10-08:00","id":1043391,"title":"","content":"In fact, one of the theories about the meaning of al-Andalus is that it was &quot;Atlantis&quot;. Although I'm not convinced about it, it could be a good Mystery for islamic mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T00:51:29-08:00","id":1043410,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, Mummy is a natural fit for this: Iberia wasn't part of the Nameless Empire, but it was damn close to their borders was likely known if not visited. That's before you factor in later migrations and conquests up through the Carthaginians, Romans, Visigoths, and Berbers, all of whom contributed to the region's history across the centuries. An Arisen on the peninsula is just as likely to be an old pagan god as they are a secret Christian saint or a secret among the Moors, and they likely last awoke for the Sothic Turn ages ago in Roman times or during one of the many religious (re)conquests. To be Arisen in such a time means navigating layers of courtly intrigue, varied ethnic groups all with deep tensions between each other, and a great many faiths, none of which look anything like the proper worship of the Judges.<br /> <br /> And all that, of course, is before the native vampires mistake you for a truly ancient elder or some worse threat to their lovely parasitic status quo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T02:00:55-08:00","id":1043423,"title":"","content":"I feel like there's a lot of ideas for everything but Vampire. Why do ya'll think that is?<br /> <br /> Maybe this question is kinda outside the scope of this thread, but does Vampire's themes resonate with the CofD audience the same way that Masquerade did to roleplayers two decades ago? Or even the same way Changeling, or Beast, seem to nowadays?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T02:06:33-08:00","id":1043425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1043423#post1043423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there's a lot of ideas for everything but Vampire. Why do ya'll think that is?<br /> <br /> Maybe this question is kinda outside the scope of this thread, but does Vampire's themes resonate with the CofD audience the same way that Masquerade did to roleplayers two decades ago? Or even the same way Changeling, or Beast, seem to nowadays?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Vampire lost a lot more fans in the switch between Masquerade and Requiem than the other lines for a lot of reasons beyond the scope of this thread, and I think that even people who would like it dismiss it as somehow the most basic or generic of them all and move onto the others, to say nothing of the line going dormant for two years after its 2e release. There's a lot more vampire fiction/media of every genre imaginable than there are for werewolves, wizards, people kidnapped and traumatized by fairies and now struggling to rebuild their lives, amnesiac Predynastic Egyptian immortals, etc, and I think folks are afraid of reinventing the wheel there when other options exist.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I think it's a damn shame. Requiem is a damn good game and one I consider an outright improvement over Masquerade, and I think that because they have to stick so close to their mortal herds and because they're functionally immortal there's more potential for them in historical setting than any other line. A product like Dark Eras is a godsend for Vampire because you can realistically have the same player characters originate in one or possibly even several.<br /> <br /> Here's hoping Dark Eras 2 gives Requiem a lot more love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T19:11:53-08:00","id":1043809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1043312#post1043312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see something with one of the Muslim kingdoms in Iberia, ideally one of the earlier ones and centered around Vampire; you got all the fun of court politics and a religion-heavy society, but from a direction the average reader isn't familiar with. It would be a chance to see some new Covenants (you could get Muslim and Jewish groups in here, plus maybe a declining Gothic group as well) beyond the pretty lazy reskins that were in <i>Ancient Mysteries</i> (which I loved, but come on; &quot;just rename the Lance and Circle and call it a day&quot; really doesn't do it justice), some fun new Bloodlines, and a chance to see formerly-Roman Kindred that fled West instead of East.<br /> <br /> You could even tack a Fall of Granada appendix onto it as a stretch goal in the same way that Requiem for Rome did for Byzantium and do vignettes where the characters or their childer react to the Reconquista and die, convert, or flee into North Africa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooooh, that's a good one, one of the few areas where you could put a Jewish covenant...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1043391#post1043391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, one of the theories about the meaning of al-Andalus is that it was &quot;Atlantis&quot;. Although I'm not convinced about it, it could be a good Mystery for islamic mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never heard that one before, I've only ever seen the Vandal--&gt;Vandalia--&gt;Vandalus--&gt;Andalus etymology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","user":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","date":". 02-04-2017, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T19:36:20-08:00","id":1043818,"title":"","content":"That's the one I find more convincing, but I've read that lately has fallen from grace among scholars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T20:24:24-08:00","id":1043833,"title":"","content":"Here's less of a Dark Era and more a seed of one; the text suggests that the Knights of Saint George's current Anglican mask is merely the latest of many, and that they have no special fondness for Christianity, so how fun would it be to see the servants of the faceless angels in another guise? My default (as it always is) is as a Roman mystery cult, but really anything before that church's establishment works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T20:31:56-08:00","id":1043838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1043833#post1043833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's less of a Dark Era and more a seed of one; the text suggests that the Knights of Saint George's current Anglican mask is merely the latest of many, and that they have no special fondness for Christianity, so how fun would it be to see the servants of the faceless angels in another guise? My default (as it always is) is as a Roman mystery cult, but really anything before that church's establishment works.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally I'd go for a gapped history rather than a continuous changing organization - with the Templars who became the Knights of St George having uncovered the Goetic Gospels in the Crusader States.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T20:43:15-08:00","id":1043841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1043838#post1043838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Personally I'd go for a gapped history rather than a continuous changing organization - with the Templars who became the Knights of St George having uncovered the Goetic Gospels in the Crusader States.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have my undivided attention. <br /> <br /> I have a soft spot for Templar stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T23:31:57-08:00","id":1043872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1041785#post1041785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bSo, as Yet Another Pitch from me: I'd love to do Industrial Revolution Werewolf in Europe, with the Uratha struggling to cope with the tidal wave of new spirit courts and colossally powerful spirit nobles birthed from the industrialisation taking place, the pollution and machinery masking the scuttling presence of a huge boom in the power of the Beshilu, and the social conflicts of the human population through whom this new era is being birthed. Iron Masters trying to chain massive industry spirit-gods into obeisance, a grand Rat Host plan to pull hellish, interstitial-place Other Cities into the world and establish a Plague Dominion, bizarre Claimed-machinery masterminds spreading their influence with every piece of track laid down for the trains that serve as their limbs and minds, human spiritualists' interference threatening the People, and the way everything fed into the demand for more raw materials, for the spreading of power, for the grasping reach of empires bourne up upon the back of industry's march.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First or Second Industrial Revolution? I'm guessing second because that's where you really get into the aesthetics associated with the era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T03:31:23-08:00","id":1043906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1043872#post1043872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> First or Second Industrial Revolution? I'm guessing second because that's where you really get into the aesthetics associated with the era.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bProbably early Second, with the slow-down between the two being a period where the Uratha were able to go 'wow, looks like we're doing alright and keeping pace with this madness, hey guys, everything's gonna be fine' only to be brutally disabused of that notion. Setting it late First still works, though; it limits the areas where one can play with ideas like Claimed steam locomotives, but they were already kicking about late First so the material can still work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T03:52:18-08:00","id":1043911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1043425#post1043425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...to say nothing of the line going dormant for two years after its 2e release...For what it's worth, I think it's a damn shame. Requiem is a damn good game and one I consider an outright improvement over Masquerade...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you. Wicked Dead and Blood &amp; Smoke really sold me on the line, and I've been waiting on the elders and Half-damned book to finish the sale.<br /> <br /> I feel like it's hard to stick an Era to because it is generic, in that it's a game about slowly degenerating into a monster - something every game more or less does but that this game <i>emphasizes</i>. It's easy when werewolves stand between two worlds and torn between two natures, mummies come from Egypt, changelings have cultural kiths, and some of the worst of real history is the basis for Hunter, but harder with vampire. Or so it seems","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T08:36:41-08:00","id":1044005,"title":"","content":"Geist: The Sacking of Rome - The end of the Roman Empire with the Visigoths sacking Rome under Alaric I. The Geists are coming in with the Visigoths after years of being used to fight barbarian wars as Atilla the Hun begins his descent into Europe. <br /> Second Sight/Mortals Mongol empire under Kublai Khan. <br /> Slasher: Turn of the century (late 1800s-1920) H.H. Holmes, Albert Fish, and Jack the Ripper. What were some of these men really hunting?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T09:19:13-08:00","id":1044017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1043425#post1043425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Vampire lost a lot more fans in the switch between Masquerade and Requiem than the other lines for a lot of reasons beyond the scope of this thread, and I think that even people who would like it dismiss it as somehow the most basic or generic of them all and move onto the others, to say nothing of the line going dormant for two years after its 2e release. There's a lot more vampire fiction/media of every genre imaginable than there are for werewolves, wizards, people kidnapped and traumatized by fairies and now struggling to rebuild their lives, amnesiac Predynastic Egyptian immortals, etc, and I think folks are afraid of reinventing the wheel there when other options exist.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I think it's a damn shame. Requiem is a damn good game and one I consider an outright improvement over Masquerade, and I think that because they have to stick so close to their mortal herds and because they're functionally immortal there's more potential for them in historical setting than any other line. A product like Dark Eras is a godsend for Vampire because you can realistically have the same player characters originate in one or possibly even several.<br /> <br /> Here's hoping Dark Eras 2 gives Requiem a lot more love.</div> </div> </div> </div>Requiem has definitely had a slow release schedule, but I don't think that's OP not wanting to touch it. We still have Half-Damned and Thousand Years of Night coming down the pipeline, so it's not like the game is dead. <br /> <br /> I'm still going to stand by Renaissance Italy for Vampire as a setting. I also wouldn't mind some of the periods mentioned in Ancient Bloodlines getting a treatment- WWI Europe, Haitian Revolution, Crusades, Ancient Persia, Ancient Egypt... there's a lot of fertile ground for Requiem to explore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T10:06:37-08:00","id":1044048,"title":"","content":"If we did Renaissance Italy, I think I'd want it to be Vampire/Demon for maximum intrigue and falling from grace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:50:31-08:00","id":1047948,"title":"","content":"I would like to see the Dark Eras - Companion as a &quot;supporting&quot; book for Dark Eras. For example interesting plots and story hooks for all the settings that where introduced in Dark Eras. (At least with the same amount of plot detail as in the God-Machine Chronicles book, would be nice. ^^)<br /> <br /> New settings should get their own Dark Eras 2. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (And maybe their own Dark Eras 2 - Companion later.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 02-12-2017, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T17:05:31-08:00","id":1047990,"title":"","content":"I am going to echo atamajakki on Roman settings for everyone. I think I'd be interested in seeing a 2e update for Requiem for Rome as a whole at some point. The feel of 2e is different from the feel of 1e and I'm curious how that would extend into a new version of RfR.<br /> <br /> I'd really like to see Mage in Alexandria. The connection with Mages and Alexander has already been seeded, and having Mages in the heart of philosophy and neoplatonism would be awesome.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see Changeling in Classical Greece. There's a reason &quot;Arcadia&quot; is used to describe the realm of the Fae. There's no place more wild and mystical than the ancient Greek countryside.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see Vampire/Changeling British Raj, or a Mage Chandragupta Maurya (which is really only a generation after To The Strongest so it could be more of a continuation of that era a la Fall of the Camarilla than a full Dark Era.) More Indian settings. It's weird how India has not been used all that much in CofD so far, with the exception of Goa in Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T17:13:03-08:00","id":1047992,"title":"","content":"The way the previous book turned out it might be feasible to do that way. Having the 'core' eras being in a set era, then Kickstarter expansions on sections or additional ones, maybe different places from the view of different splats, or showing one group during the fall or rise.<br /> <br /> I couldn't say whether Rome was popular enough to warrant it, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-12-2017, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T02:30:19-08:00","id":1048137,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Beast in Pre-Colonial Australia could be pretty cool. Not only because it's a land where everything can kill you (lots of inspiration for potential horrors), but also because it's a land where you can beasts and geotia drifting along the Songlines. It's a time and place where the lessons a beast is meant to teach isn't outdated, it's the true time when a beast's lessons actually could be the difference between life and death. You can tap into Dreamtime not because it's called Dreamtime, but because it is an immaterial place that is made of thought and story and warning. Also, you can have it interact with the ghost-wolves discussed in WtF 2e, where the beasts gained nightmares from the ghost-wolves, and the ghost-wolves learned how to communicate through dreams from interacting with beasts (resulting in the formulation of the Dream Lodge).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Changeling in 1930-40's Australia. Sort of the opposite situation to the Grimm Dark Era, it is in a time where thousands of stories died and were lost as aboriginal australian's lost the possibility of passing on their culture to the new generations, causing many fae to become desperate and for the hedge to be changing to take on a mix of folklore from migrants. In addition, this was in the middle of the great depression, leading to unemployment going as high as 25% to 29% (depending on what source you look at), meaning gentry could do things like grant boons to mortals in return for doing rituals which keep their (now fading) narrative alive or can offer the person a &quot;job&quot; and take them as a &quot;willing&quot; servant to arcadia meaning their might be a decent amount of loyalists. The era can also reference similiarities between changelings and the stolen generation, but... Doing that would require being very very careful.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Promethean in Gold Rush Australia. Where the flood of immigrants from all over (especially china) caused the country to truly start to be multicultural, the created have perfect </span>opportunity<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> to travel to a country which was still young and still refining itself. It was a time where being a nomad wouldn't be seen as odd, meaning prometheans can prevent wastelands without standing out as strangers. Also it gives prometheans a great chance to see desperation and hope is such an extreme way. Lastly, alchemists would probably make decent use of all the gold, and even </span>if the alchemists are out their for gold, disquiet and desperation <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">can lead to alchemists becoming a considerable problem for the Created who are lured to the gold fields.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-13-2017, 05:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T04:16:05-08:00","id":1048166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1048137#post1048137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[FONT=inherit]Beast in Pre-Colonial Australia could be pretty cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>STOP STEALING MY IDEAS... uh, I mean, great minds think alike, milo <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T12:13:02-08:00","id":1048374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1047948#post1047948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see the Dark Eras - Companion as a &amp;quot;supporting&amp;quot; book for Dark Eras. For example interesting plots and story hooks for all the settings that where introduced in Dark Eras. (At least with the same amount of plot detail as in the God-Machine Chronicles book, would be nice. ^^)<br /> <br /> New settings should get their own Dark Eras 2. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (And maybe their own Dark Eras 2 - Companion later.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a little late for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T13:11:40-08:00","id":1048402,"title":"","content":"One of my intended settings for Changeling 2e is Golden Age of Piracy Freehold of Nassau, due to the massive world of naval superstition and the interplay of folk legend and history that made up that time period, and I think that would be a pretty cool official Dark Era. So throwing that out there, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T13:38:45-08:00","id":1048407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1048402#post1048402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my intended settings for Changeling 2e is Golden Age of Piracy Freehold of Nassau, due to the massive world of naval superstition and the interplay of folk legend and history that made up that time period, and I think that would be a pretty cool official Dark Era. So throwing that out there, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the syncretic nature of pirate folklore demands at least partly Geist content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T14:14:55-08:00","id":1048417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1048407#post1048407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the syncretic nature of pirate folklore demands at least partly Geist content.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd be &quot;on board&quot; with that, were it not for the fact that Dead Men Tell No Tales.<br /> <br /> <b>/banned six posts in</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T14:21:07-08:00","id":1048419,"title":"","content":"I would love to see a Mississippi Steamboat era for Vampire, set before the American civil war. Plantation slavery is at its height. Political discourse is going to bubble over into war. Old traditions are being challenged by new ideals and steamboats allow an easy method of trade and travel for Kindred, although the boats themselves will become obsolete within a generation. The combination of brutality and courtly veneer is very vampire and ripe for a southern Gothic treatment, Requiem style. You could play up plantation owning elders against abolitionist neonates. New Orleans would be brought back as a signature city.<br /> To keep the setting being too dark, I would portray vampire society as largely wanting to keep their herds healthy since disease could easily decimate mortal populations and most vampires would want to avoid seeing their food source disappear. This would incentivize most vampires to feed carefully. This would lend a certain dramatic irony to proceedings since compared to the depredations and casual brutality of human society, most vampires wouldn't be too bad.<br /> <br /> I'd also love to see Mughal India Changeling. To be honest almost any Indian historical setting would suit me but it definitely should be for Changeling!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T15:15:13-08:00","id":1048442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1048402#post1048402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my intended settings for Changeling 2e is Golden Age of Piracy Freehold of Nassau, due to the massive world of naval superstition and the interplay of folk legend and history that made up that time period, and I think that would be a pretty cool official Dark Era. So throwing that out there, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it's also already been mentioned as a pretty big deal in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T16:01:05-08:00","id":1048456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1048442#post1048442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe it's also already been mentioned as a pretty big deal in Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes you are right! I remember the Nassau Pirate Republic mentioned somewhere in Mage, but I forget exactly where. Sounds like a great time period for a lot of different settings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T23:25:13-08:00","id":1048605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1048456#post1048456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes you are right! I remember the Nassau Pirate Republic mentioned somewhere in Mage, but I forget exactly where. Sounds like a great time period for a lot of different settings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In <b>Mage</b>, Nassau Pirate Republic is made of democratic Nameless Order that Seers of Throne AND Silver Ladder want's to crush.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T01:46:01-08:00","id":1048630,"title":"","content":"I don't know what era I want, but anything that gets me more Mummy I am game for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T07:52:42-08:00","id":1048749,"title":"","content":"Nassau Navigations would be awesome.<br /> <br /> I'm biased though, as I was born and live in one of the cities that were governed by him in the mid 1600s, Recife, Brazil.<br /> <br /> The history of the Jews that accompanied him is specially interesting.<br /> <br /> When the Portuguese took back the city, Jews, which were mostly engineers, doctors, lawyers and bankers fled the Portuguese religious persecution.<br /> <br /> 16 ships departed Recife, 15 made it back to Holland, one was captured by Spanish pirates then rescued by a French ship and released in New Amsterdam, which is known today as New York.<br /> <br /> Imagine the Fate plots in that!<br /> <br /> Our city is home to the first synagogue of the Americas, which today is a museum. (Services there still occur, but can only be attended by ultra orthodox jews. A friend of mine from a different state was very upset when he tried to attend and was denied entrance for being too &quot;modern&quot;.)<br /> <br /> Many people here still lament Nassau's and the Jews' departure. We would be a very different people/country had they stayed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 02-14-2017, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T09:29:26-08:00","id":1048780,"title":"","content":"More South American settings are always appreciated. They never get much love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:01:36-08:00","id":1050951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1048374#post1048374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a little late for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. If you are already creating a book with more new settings you could easily rename it to Dark Eras 2. But that is not the point..<br /> I would like to see interesting plot ideas to support the storyteller. And yes, I would prefer a clean separation like I mentioned, but this is the &quot;ideal&quot; solution in my opinion. They could also split the book and add a plot section, or whatever. There are already so many good settings in the first book, that I think that the whole &quot;Dark Eras&quot; materials would be more enhanced by good plot ideas instead of new settings. <br /> However this does not mean, that I don't understand that other people want to see a certain setting in the next book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:33:16-08:00","id":1050966,"title":"","content":"Post ww2 Vienna for demon and post ww1 Paris for changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T09:26:39-08:00","id":1051022,"title":"","content":"I would love Angkor as a setting!<br /> Spread over an area larger than modern day New York City, with up to a million inhabitants, it was an enourmous centre of culture and trade - from the 9th to the 15th century. Towards the end, it was the largest metropolitan area of the world at the time! Even the Chinese were impressed with what the markets of Angkor offered - the Khmer were masterful traders and craftsman. At the same time, the culture faced problems: a climate change that threatened their current methods of transportation and access to water, pride, religious dispute (Hinduism was being replaced by Buddhism, and the new leaders wanted to show off, prove that they were richer and better then the previous ones), a rising rival power in the Thai...<br /> I see quite some potential for Changeling there, but I think Demon would work rather well, too. In addition, with such riches and rare materials available, I can see bands of Hunters coming all the way, just to stack up on necessities for hunting down their target. Vampire, Mage or Beast would work in the setting, too, but imo Changeling, Demon and Hunters have the most potential here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T18:05:26-08:00","id":1051253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1050966#post1050966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">post ww1 Paris for changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>YES. I actually suggested this to a friend of mine a few weeks ago and I completely forgot. Changeling: The Lost [Generation] would be amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T04:21:41-08:00","id":1052492,"title":"","content":"Considering that this thread also also about things in general I would like to see and not only a specific Era, here is one of those- I want a Mage Era (no matter which) that have detailed mechanics for the previous Orders of the Diamond (that is, the Keeper of the World, the Pancryptiats and the Tremere as full blown Order).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T04:41:02-08:00","id":1052497,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see an Era about the emergence of Ventrue. Not necessarily their origins, but how they affected kindred society and how kindred society would look like after the fall of the Camarilla. Where the Ventrue actually came from could rather be used as a set of story seeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T08:39:08-08:00","id":1052584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1052492#post1052492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that this thread also also about things in general I would like to see and not only a specific Era, here is one of those- I want a Mage Era (no matter which) that have detailed mechanics for the previous Orders of the Diamond (that is, the Keeper of the World, the Pancryptiats and the Tremere as full blown Order).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think to remember that Dave said the Pancryptiates and the Keepers splats will be in Dark Eras 2.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T09:26:50-08:00","id":1052602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1052497#post1052497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see an Era about the emergence of Ventrue. Not necessarily their origins, but how they affected kindred society and how kindred society would look like after the fall of the Camarilla. Where the Ventrue actually came from could rather be used as a set of story seeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like this, but it's purely personal preference. I really, really love how the Ventrue are just kind of there after the Fall of the Camarilla totally usurping the role of the Julii and there is zero explanation. I'm sure it can be done well, and I'd happily read it and devour it, but the Ventrue just kind of taking the place of the Julii with total explanation left to the ST is one of my favorite parts of Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T09:34:51-08:00","id":1052605,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't go so far as to say there's zero explanation, there's plenty of hints, just no clear-cut description of how it happened. Which, like you, I think fits.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a suitable compromise would be the rising of another clan that has gone extinct, or maybe the death of a more prominent clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-21-2017, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T10:05:10-08:00","id":1052614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1052605#post1052605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't go so far as to say there's zero explanation, there's plenty of hints, just no clear-cut description of how it happened. Which, like you, I think fits.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a suitable compromise would be the rising of another clan that has gone extinct, or maybe the death of a more prominent clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright sure, there isn't ZERO explanation. There are many explanations (The Ventrue are the Traditores! The Ventrue predate the Julii! The Julii were a Ventrue bloodline! The Julii were actually a GANGREL Bloodline! The Ventrue just ARE FLAT OUT the Julii, but the Strix didn't destroy them. Yet.) just no definitive one.<br /> <br /> I like that there's no definitive one. But I'd be lying if I said I wouldn't still buy and read The Rise of the Ventrue. I just kind of don't want there to be it.<br /> <br /> I would like to see other extinct Clans, though. Or perhaps just have another Dark Era set somewhere else in the Roman Empire than Rome itself, with the Julii back as one of the five clans. That'd be pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T11:26:22-08:00","id":1052650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1050966#post1050966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Post ww2 Vienna for demon...</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The Third Man </i>as a <b>Demon</b> chronicle! Why have I never thought of this?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T11:27:25-08:00","id":1052651,"title":"","content":"As I wrote I didn't ask for an explanation for where the Ventrue came from. That works best as completely optional story seeds. Rather, how the integration and rise of Ventrue as a clan could definitely use some attention. Just remember that a Dark Era also focuses on a certain geographical area as well meaning Ventrue in other places may have completely different kinds of interactions with the other clans.<br /> <br /> Edit: For example, the spread of Ventrues to the New World would have a lot more culture vs culture as they come with the European conquistadores and explorers, while Ventrues in Italy might have to fight for a new clan identity in order to get accepted. Anyone who mistakes them for Julii would certainly fear the return of the Birds of Dis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-21-2017, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T09:48:40-08:00","id":1053286,"title":"","content":"To revive an idea I once tried to run but didn't have the group for: New France in the mid-1700s, with the Seven Years' War driving conflict between France and Britain, as a Vampire setting. You get all sorts of fun toys (a possible prelude to the Montreal setting, pirates and privateers, some of the important figures of the American Revolution), and can frame it as a mirrored conflict among the dead, with the Sanctified backing French Catholic colonial efforts and the Invictus standing behind British mercantile interests, as well as a chance to highlight native vampires as the largely dominant power, possible with now-vanished Clans, Bloodlines, Disciplines, and Blood Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T12:17:14-08:00","id":1053364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1053286#post1053286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To revive an idea I once tried to run but didn't have the group for: New France in the mid-1700s, with the Seven Years' War driving conflict between France and Britain, as a Vampire setting. You get all sorts of fun toys (a possible prelude to the Montreal setting, pirates and privateers, some of the important figures of the American Revolution), and can frame it as a mirrored conflict among the dead, with the Sanctified backing French Catholic colonial efforts and the Invictus standing behind British mercantile interests, as well as a chance to highlight native vampires as the largely dominant power, possible with now-vanished Clans, Bloodlines, Disciplines, and Blood Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would spend all of the money on this. Colonial New World is my jam. Vampires are also my jam. Jam squared.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T09:43:05-08:00","id":1054349,"title":"","content":"I would love to see more Vampire stuff like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12981_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12981\" data-vbnamecard=\"12981\">RomulusGloriosus</a>. Especially colonial Vampire, XVIII, XIX century. Together with my friends we played in Europe and USA for many years. It's good to make some changes.<br /> More about Dracula or Dracula's brides, Eastern Europe in XVI, XVII century would be cool, too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T14:10:44-08:00","id":1057759,"title":"","content":"I do really hope Jazz Age Vampire gets another crack at things. It would be such a fun time period to romp around in; a talented author could do some super evocative stuff with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T14:23:49-08:00","id":1057764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1057759#post1057759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do really hope Jazz Age Vampire gets another crack at things. It would be such a fun time period to romp around in; a talented author could do some super evocative stuff with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Joint Vampire/Changeling in the 20s? &quot;Jazz Age&quot; Vampire, &quot;Lost Generation&quot; Lost?<br /> <br /> I've actually run a Vampire game set in the 20s before. It jives well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T22:14:15-08:00","id":1057936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1052497#post1052497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see an Era about the emergence of Ventrue. Not necessarily their origins, but how they affected kindred society and how kindred society would look like after the fall of the Camarilla. Where the Ventrue actually came from could rather be used as a set of story seeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm wondering if this will be shown in the Black Death Era in the Companion.<br /> <br /> I'm trying hard to think of Mummy Eras (no other Eras matter) and I'm reminded of DaveB's campaign he set in India. One of the PCs sought Apotheosis in previous Descents, and made the connection between Deathless experience and Buddhist reincarnation. That would be an interesting setting and theme to explore for <b>Mummy</b>, and you could even include Thuggee cults that are completely racist, ahistorical, and scandalous! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T06:20:07-08:00","id":1058018,"title":"","content":"Jazz age vampire / changeling and Mississippi steamboat vampire really gets my interest. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11247-bluenose","name":"Bluenose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T06:26:13-08:00","id":1060051,"title":"","content":"I haven't read any Dark Eras stuff yet but is there any Werewolf / Viking stuff? I think that kind of association could be a lot of fun to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T06:42:44-08:00","id":1060054,"title":"","content":"The Wolf and the Raven<br /> (Also includes Sin-Eaters.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T07:48:55-08:00","id":1060077,"title":"","content":"And it is excellent. One of my favourite eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T11:57:37-08:00","id":1060206,"title":"","content":"Lots of great ideas here! Personally I have a few preferences:<br /> <br /> 1 Specific eras - Would love to see some Celtic eras e.g. the &quot;real&quot; Arthurian Britain (late 5th C after the fall of Rome), or in the time of the potato famine and exodus to the US. Also, while i agree that more non-European/North american stuff would be nice there are lots of such eras that would be great to explore. Especially there are European countries that get little focus but may have some really interesting history, some really well known (Romania in the time of the real Vlad the Impaler) and other stuff much less so (Prague under communism?). Also some focus on religious or cultural groups within European and North american society that may not get much focus in regular rpg settings (e.g. eras of the Jewish diaspora). <br /> <br /> 2 More eras with material for more than one factions, preferably at least 2 or three. I mostly play mage so i was a bit disappointed that that there was no indication of how to use mage in eras other than the ones specific to that line. I would love to run mage in Viking times, Colonial era Salem and 17th C France but there were no notes for that. I would love to see something more like the notes at the back of several of the new 5E D&amp;D in which they present the adventure for Forgotten Realms but provide notes on how to adapt to different D&amp;D campaign worlds. But the notes would be for what different factions were doing in that era and provide guidance on how those groups might interact with the primary group or groups presented. <br /> <br /> 3 Maybe a look at one or more settings with a look at different eras for that setting. That way a storyteller can trace the occult history of one area over time. e.g. Israel in ancient times, in the Crusades, under the Ottoman empire, and under the British mandate. Or Rome in the Roman empire, in the renaissance, in the 19th in the age of unification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T12:45:10-08:00","id":1060231,"title":"","content":"On a slight tangent some suggestions for other rpg resources for running NWoD or Chronicles of darkness in interesting eras:<br /> <br /> 1 Mythic Britain (for Runequest) and Keltia rpg are great resources for Arthurian flavored Celtic dark ages Britain.<br /> <br /> 2 Savage worlds Pirates of the Spanish main for Pirate age<br /> <br /> 3 Witch Hunter the Invisible world for Colonial America and much of the rest of the world in the 17th C<br /> <br /> 4 World War Cthulhu, Savage Worlds Weird War 2 and Achtung Cthulhu for WW2<br /> <br /> 5 Lex Occultum - Currently on Kickstarter from the same Swedish company that is producing Trudvang. 18th C with a campaign specifically included for 18th C Paris","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12792,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","user":"scifirabbi","date":". 03-08-2017, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T15:09:21-08:00","id":1060303,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1060206#post1060206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of great ideas here! Personally I have a few preferences:<br /> <br /> 2 More eras with material for more than one factions, preferably at least 2 or three. I mostly play mage so i was a bit disappointed that that there was no indication of how to use mage in eras other than the ones specific to that line. I would love to run mage in Viking times, Colonial era Salem and 17th C France but there were no notes for that. I would love to see something more like the notes at the back of several of the new 5E D&amp;D in which they present the adventure for Forgotten Realms but provide notes on how to adapt to different D&amp;D campaign worlds. But the notes would be for what different factions were doing in that era and provide guidance on how those groups might interact with the primary group or groups presented.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this very, very much. Most of the crossover Eras were written as &quot;here's what one gameline and another gameline were up to at the time,&quot; with very little thematic or narrative mesh between them. If we see a Vampire/Changeling setting, I want to see what Covenants are buddies with what Courts, and if membership bleeds across or how you can play both in the same group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T15:52:50-08:00","id":1060322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1060303#post1060303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seconding this very, very much. Most of the crossover Eras were written as &quot;here's what one gameline and another gameline were up to at the time,&quot; with very little thematic or narrative mesh between them. If we see a Vampire/Changeling setting, I want to see what Covenants are buddies with what Courts, and if membership bleeds across or how you can play both in the same group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't say enough how much I <i>don't </i>want that, because crossovers give me hives.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'd love to see more settings where there's more than one venue represented (such as Requiem for Regina, The Sundered World, etc.) so that people who say &quot;Yes! The Fall of Constantinople is my favorite time period!&quot; can have more options besides Demon, if Demon isn't their thing. (That was just a random sample, nothing against After The Fall or Demon.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T18:10:39-08:00","id":1060358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1060322#post1060322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't say enough how much I <i>don't </i>want that, because crossovers give me hives.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'd love to see more settings where there's more than one venue represented (such as Requiem for Regina, The Sundered World, etc.) so that people who say &quot;Yes! The Fall of Constantinople is my favorite time period!&quot; can have more options besides Demon, if Demon isn't their thing. (That was just a random sample, nothing against After The Fall or Demon.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm opposed to kitchen sink crossover, but if you limit it to two gamelines and drill down on shared themes or cosmology, there's a lot of potential there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T19:47:43-07:00","id":1062136,"title":"","content":"Corrections being added in. We are getting there people!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T07:55:17-07:00","id":1083969,"title":"","content":"Thought I'd bump this thread with some of my own suggestions: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Werewolf/Hunter: Baltic Crusades, Livonian and Prussian specifically.</li> <li>Mortal (is this still a thing?): Early Protestant Reformation in England and Germany.</li> <li>Mage/Promethean: Prague during reign of Rudolph II.</li> <li>Mage: Late 18th century Bavaria.</li> <li>Werewolf: French and Indian War.</li> <li>Vampire/Hunter: Prohibition era New York/Chicago.</li> </ol><br /> Whadya think? I expect the reasoning for each speaks for itself, but I can elaborate if anyone finds the choices confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T19:13:40-07:00","id":1086002,"title":"","content":"Baltic Crusades would be pretty awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T08:12:21-07:00","id":1086641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1086002#post1086002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baltic Crusades would be pretty awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark forests, Gothic castles, Pagans still worshiping the &quot;Old Gods&quot;, Powerful Knightly Orders, what's not to love?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T09:52:53-07:00","id":1086677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1086641#post1086641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dark forests, Gothic castles, Pagans still worshiping the &quot;Old Gods&quot;, Powerful Knightly Orders, what's not to love?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which game-line(s), though? Beast (see above), Hunter (travel to new lands, meet new people and kill their monsters), Mage (strong showings for Adamantine Arrow, Mysterium, and Silver Ladder, with some Seer manipulation on the side), Geist (massive death tends to draw/create Sin-Eaters), Promethean (it is kinda a Pilgrimage)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T10:59:20-07:00","id":1086711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1086677#post1086677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Which game-line(s), though? Beast (see above), Hunter (travel to new lands, meet new people and kill their monsters), Mage (strong showings for Adamantine Arrow, Mysterium, and Silver Ladder, with some Seer manipulation on the side), Geist (massive death tends to draw/create Sin-Eaters), Promethean (it is kinda a Pilgrimage)?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the list I posted on the previous page, which I assume Second Chances was responding to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040309-what-do-you-want-out-of-dark-eras-2?p=1083969#post1083969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Werewolf/Hunter: Baltic Crusades, Livonian and Prussian specifically.</li> <li>Mortal (is this still a thing?): Early Protestant Reformation in England and Germany.</li> <li>Mage/Promethean: Prague during reign of Rudolph II.</li> <li>Mage: Late 18th century Bavaria.</li> <li>Werewolf: French and Indian War.</li> <li>Vampire/Hunter: Prohibition era New York/Chicago.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that the Baltic Crusades were best for Werewolf and Hunter. The region was an untamed, primitive wilderness (or at least the crusaders probably saw it that way) where practice of pantheistic religions was still common, a perhaps safer place for werewolves to dwell in the uncertain times of Christianity's spread. We could also see how the Crusades, and the gradual Christianization of the Pagans would affect the spirit worlds. During the Crusades against the Pagans several Holy Orders were established, most notably the Teutonic and Livonian Orders. They erected great Castles and gained enough power that they effectively became their own states. This would be an interesting place to explore Hunter organizations, as well as introduce new compact or conspiracies for other sects of Christianity. (We've only seen Catholic and American Evangelical groups in the Hunter books so far, no Orthodox groups. The Baltic Crusades happened right on the doorstep of Orthodox Christendom and Orthodox realms like Novgorod would often butt-heads with the new Holy orders.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}